[0.022,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[38;5;174m ▐\u001b[48;5;16m▛███▛█\u001b[12G\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[1mClaude Code\u001b[24G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246mv2.1.325\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;174m▝▜\u001b[48;5;16m█\u001b[7G█\u001b[49m█▀\u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;246mdeepseek-flash[\u001b[28Gm] · API Usage Billing\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;174m ▝▝   ▝▝ \u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;246m/work\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mPlease implement this issue.\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                              \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m#26 The summary of one month\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                            \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mAt the end of each month accounting closes the books, and wants the summary of the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Binvoices issued in\u001b[22Gtha\u001b[26G month. Add \u001b[38;5;153m--month <YYYY-MM>\u001b[38;5;231m to \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer summary\u001b[38;5;231m: with\u001b[82Git,\u001b[86Gthe \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bsummary covers only the\u001b[27Ginvoices issued in that month, such as \u001b[38;5;153m--month 2026-10\u001b[38;5;231m.\u001b[39m        \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B                                                                               \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- Without \u001b[38;5;153m--month\u001b[38;5;231m, the summary prints exactly what it prints today.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BA month\u001b[13Gnot written a\u001b[27G YYYY-MM \u001b[37Gs an error that names \u001b[60Gt.\u001b[39m        \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m \u001b[3G\u001b[39mReading\u001b[11Gsrc/report/aging.ts\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m ⎿  \u001b[39m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mNow design implementation. I'll add filter function and month validation. Naming: \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m     \u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mforMonth\u001b[39m to parallel \u001b[38;5;153mforCustomer\u001b[39m. Error \u001b[38;5;153mInvalidMonthError\u001b[39m. Message should name the \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bmonth: \u001b[38;5;153mmonth \"2026-1\" is not written as YYYY-MM\u001b[39m or \u001b[38;5;153m\"2026-1\" is not a month written as\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BYYYY-MM\u001b[39m. The option is \u001b[38;5;153m--month\u001b[39m; the error should name it. If InvalidMonthError is \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bthrown from filter, message could be: \u001b[38;5;153m\"2026-1\" is not written as YYYY-MM\u001b[39m. In cli \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Boutput: \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer: \"2026-1\" is not written as YYYY-MM\u001b[39m. That names it. Maybe clearer: \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153m--month \"2026-1\" is not written as YYYY-MM\u001b[39m. But then filter leaks CLI naming. \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BAlternatively error message \u001b[38;5;153mmonth \"2026-1\" is not written as YYYY-MM\u001b[39m. That names it \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Band is clear. I'll use that. Exit code: I'll treat as UsageError output with usage \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Band exit 2. Need \u001b[38;5;153mInvalidMonthError\u001b[39m imported in cli.…\r\u001b[37C\u001b[2B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246mthought for 6s)\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
